.²1 The mind, heart, understanding, perception, intelligence; as in {#sumanas, dumarnas#} <ab>&c.</ab>
.²2 (In <ab>phil.</ab>) The mind or internal organ of perception and cognition,
 the instrument by which objects of sense affect the soul; (in Nyāya <ab>phil.</ab>
 {#manas#} is regarded as a Dravya or substance, and is distinct from {#Atman#}
 or the soul); {#tadeva suKaduHKAdyupalabDisADanamindriyaM pratijIvaM#}
 {#BinnamaRu nityaM ca#} <ls>Tarka K.</ls>
.²3 Conscience, the faculty of discrimination or judgment.
.²4 Thought, idea, fancy, imagination, conception; {#paSyannadUrAnmanasApyaDfzyam#}
 <ls>Ku. 3. 51</ls>; <ls>R. 2. 27</ls>; {#kAyena vAcA manasApi SaSvat#} <ls n="R.">5. 5</ls>; {#manasApi#}
 {#na vipriyaM mayA#} ({#kftapUrvam#}) <ls n="R.">8. 52</ls>.
.²5 Design, purpose, intention.
.²6 Will, wish, desire, inclination; in this sense {#manas#} is frequently
 used with the infinitive form with the final {#m#} dropped, and forms
 adjectives; {#ayaM janaH prazwumanAstapoDane#} <ls>Ku. 5. 40</ls>; <ab>cf.</ab> {#kAma#}.
.²7 Reflection ({#DyAna#}); {#manasA japEH praRatiBiH prayataH samupeyivAnaDipatiM#}
 {#sa divaH#} <ls>Ki. 6. 22</ls>.
.²8 Disposition, temper, mood.
.²9 Spirit, energy, mettle; {#manovIryavarotsiktamasfRyamakutoBayam#} <ls>Bhāg. 3. 17. 22</ls>.
.²10 <ab>N.</ab> of the lake called Mānasa.
.²11 Breath or living soul.
.²12 Desire, longing after. ({#manasA gam#} <ab>&c.</ab> to think of, contemplate,
 remember; {#jagAma manasA rAmaM DarmajYo DarmakANkzayA#} <ls>Rām. 2. 82. 9</ls>;
